{
  "slug": "ddw",
  "name": "Ddw",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A development harness for Claude Code that enforces disciplined workflows — decisions before code, tasks before implementation. Includes architect review, automated QA, drift detection, and shell hooks that physically block rule violations.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **11 skills**, **4 agents** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (11): `architect` (Run an architectural design review for a feature, or bootstrap a project's guardrails and invariants), `close` (Run the mandatory post-done checklist after Owner sets a task to done), `decision` (Create a new decision file and add it to the DECISION_LOG), `drift` (Check spec-code consistency), `ideate` (Guide structured thinking to produce a PRD document), `init` (Bootstrap the Decision-Driven Workflow into a project), `qa` (Run automated QA against acceptance criteria + invariants), `review` (Review a task's completion criteria, run tests, walk through the owner checklist, and batch-tick results), and 3 more\n- **Agents** (4): `architect`, `developer`, `qa`, `shaper`\n- **Hooks** (4): `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ddw@claude-community` from `inalps/ddw`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 11,
    "agent": 4,
    "hook": 4
  },
